local _, ns = ...
local E = ns.DB.entries
E["npc:ringo"] = {t="npc",n="Ringo",z="ungoro",s="Ringo is an unfortunate goblin explorer who ventured up the blistering heights of Fire Plume Ridge in Un'Goro Crater. Overwhelmed by the volcano's stifling heat and noxious vapors, he collapsed inside a cave, desperate for someone to help him back down. His close friend Spraggle Frock remains worried sick back at Marshal's Refuge.",h="Ringo is an unfortunate goblin explorer who ventured up the blistering heights of Fire Plume Ridge in Un'Goro...",sec={{t="A Venture Too Close to the Flame",b="While goblins are known for braving hazardous environments in search of wealth or oddities, Fire Plume Ridge proves harsh even by their standards. Towering in the center of Un'Goro Crater, the active volcano spews ash, magma, and boiling steam. Ringo climbed about halfway up the southern face before the suffocating heat finally proved too much for him. Leaving his belongings scattered just outside, he crawled into a cave to shelter from the sweltering atmosphere, completely incapacitated by heat exhaustion.",sp=0},{t="A Grueling Trek Down the Slopes",b="Getting Ringo off the mountain is an ordeal in itself. The goblin is so weakened by dehydration and heatstroke that he repeatedly faints along the descent. Keeping him on his feet requires liberal splashes from a canteen—or an occasional brisk slap across the face to shake him conscious. Escorting him past the mountain's volatile elementals and predators all the way back to the safety of Marshal's Refuge requires constant vigilance until he can be reunited with his friend Spraggle.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Ringo?",a="Ringo is a goblin explorer in Un'Goro Crater who climbed up the volcanic slopes of Fire Plume Ridge, only to succumb to intense heat exhaustion inside a cave.",al={"ringo","who is ringo","ringo goblin"}},{q="Where is Ringo located?",a="He can be found resting inside a south-facing cave roughly halfway up the slopes of Fire Plume Ridge, in the center of Un'Goro Crater.",al={"ringo location","where is ringo","find ringo"}},{q="Who is looking for Ringo?",a="His good friend Spraggle Frock, who is stationed at Marshal's Refuge in northern Un'Goro, is deeply concerned about Ringo's disappearance.",al={"who is spraggle","ringo friend","spraggle frock"}},{q="Why keeps fainting on the way down?",a="Ringo is suffering from severe heat exhaustion and dehydration caused by the active volcanic heat and fumes of Fire Plume Ridge. Spraggle's canteen is needed to wake him up whenever he passes out.",al={"why does ringo faint","ringo passing out","ringo collapses"}},{q="What is Ringo's Sack?",a="It is Ringo's personal pack, which he dropped just outside the mouth of his cave when he collapsed from the heat before retreating inside.",al={"ringo's sack","ringo bag","lost bag ringo"}},{q="Where does Ringo need to go?",a="He needs a safe escort off the volcano and across the crater floor to Marshal's Refuge, where his friend Spraggle Frock is waiting.",al={"where do i take ringo","ringo destination","ringo escort end"}}},kw={"fire plume ridge","goblin","heat exhaustion","marshal's stand","ringo","spraggle frock","un'goro crater"},rel={"subzone:fire-plume-ridge","zone:ungoro","topic:goblin"},src={"Ringo"}}
E["npc:torwa-pathfinder"] = {t="npc",n="Torwa Pathfinder",z="ungoro",s="Torwa Pathfinder is a lone tauren hunter and tracker camped at the entrance to Un'Goro Crater, just below the ramp descending from Tanaris. He observes the basin's primordial wildlife, studying the dangerous predators that rule the jungle floor. Adventurers seeking to test their mettle against the crater's legendary beasts often seek his guidance.",h="Torwa Pathfinder is a lone tauren hunter and tracker camped at the entrance to Un'Goro Crater, just below the...",sec={{t="Watcher at the Threshold",b="Perched at the eastern base of the crater where the desert sands of Tanaris give way to humid jungle steam, Torwa Pathfinder serves as an informal warden for newcomers. He respects the wild forces of Un'Goro, understanding that careless wanderers quickly become fodder for the local fauna. His campsite provides a rare moment of respite before travelers dive into the sweltering depths.",sp=0},{t="The Hunt for Lar'korwi",b="Much of Torwa's attention is consumed by Lar'korwi, a notoriously cunning and fierce raptor roaming the northern reaches of the crater. Torwa understands that brute strength alone cannot bring down such an apex predator. Instead, he instructs hunters to study its feeding habits, using fresh carcase meat and glands to craft a bait potent enough to lure the beast out into the open.",sp=0},{t="Primal Poisons and Beasts",b="Beyond hunting the crater's apex raptors, Torwa maintains a deep curiosity regarding the toxic flora and aggressive ape colonies that inhabit the basin. He directs travelers to harvest venom from volatile bloodpetals and observe the strength of dominant beasts like the mighty gorilla U'cha, constantly analyzing how nature's deadliest adaptations function in isolation.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Torwa Pathfinder?",a="Torwa is camped near the eastern edge of Un'Goro Crater, right near the base of the winding ramp that climbs up into the desert of Tanaris.",al={"torwa location","where is torwa","find torwa pathfinder"}},{q="What is Lar'korwi?",a="Lar'korwi is a legendary and elusive raptor stalking Un'Goro Crater. Renowned for its ferocity and cunning, it cannot easily be tracked by normal means and must be lured out using specialized bait.",al={"larkorwi","who is larkorwi","what is larkorwi"}},{q="Does Torwa only offer quests to Horde players?",a="No. Despite being a tauren, Torwa Pathfinder acts independently in the wilderness. He offers his tracking wisdom and hunting challenges to capable adventurers of both the Alliance and the Horde.",al={"is torwa horde only","can alliance talk to torwa","torwa faction"}},{q="Why is Torwa interested in Bloodpetals?",a="Torwa is fascinated by the lethal defenses of Un'Goro's native plants. He asks adventurers to collect secretions from aggressive bloodpetals to understand and test the potency of their natural toxins.",al={"bloodpetal quest","why bloodpetals","torwa poison"}},{q="Who is U'cha?",a="U'cha is an exceptionally powerful gorilla residing in the caves and ape territories of Un'Goro. Torwa challenges hunters to defeat U'cha to prove their prowess against the basin's strongest beasts.",al={"mighty u'cha","gorilla boss ungoro","ucha quest"}},{q="Is Torwa Pathfinder related to Nura Pathfinder?",a="They share the Pathfinder surname, suggesting a kinship among tauren trackers, though Torwa remains focused entirely on the perilous wilderness of Un'Goro.",al={"nura pathfinder","torwa family","pathfinder family"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="Torwa embodies the patience and craft of a master tracker, demonstrating that luring an apex predator requires understanding its diet, scent, and territorial habits rather than relying on raw force.",["race:Tauren"]="For wandering tauren, finding Torwa at the edge of the crater is a reassuring reminder of their people's reverence for nature, even amidst the prehistoric chaos of Un'Goro."},kw={"bloodpetal","lar'korwi","pathfinder","raptor","tanaris","torwa","u'cha","ungoro"},rel={"zone:ungoro","zone:tanaris","topic:tauren"},src={"Torwa Pathfinder"}}
E["npc:williden-marshal"] = {t="npc",n="Williden Marshal",z="ungoro",s="Williden Marshal is the ambitious human leader of Marshal's Expedition, based out of Marshal's Refuge in northern Un'Goro Crater. Driven by the lure of rare flora, mysterious crystals, and profitable scientific research, he brought his team into the crater only to watch their lower camps overrun by the basin's colossal beasts.",h="Williden Marshal is the ambitious human leader of Marshal's Expedition, based out of Marshal's Refuge in...",sec={{t="A Precarious Foothold",b="Williden Marshal brought an entire scientific expedition deep into Un'Goro Crater seeking fortune and discovery. Intrigued by accounts of alien crystals, uncataloged plants, and untapped resources, he established multiple forward camps across the valley floor. However, the primeval wilderness quickly turned against them. Ravenous devilsaurs, encroaching silithid, and primal beasts dismantled their research posts, forcing Williden and his survivors to retreat up into the northern cliffs to establish Marshal's Refuge.",sp=0},{t="Salvaging the Dream",b="Despite being driven to the crater's mountainous edge, Williden refuses to pack up and abandon his investment. From the relative safety of the refuge, he hires passing adventurers to delve back into the savage lowlands to recover lost food crates, expensive scientific instruments, and his personal expedition journal. Though often known simply as 'Wil' to close comrades like Spark Nilminer, he takes the venture seriously—insisting on recovering their work even as titanic predators stalk the valley beneath them.",sp=0},{t="Family Ties",b="Williden is part of a family of ambitious frontier explorers hailing from the Eastern Kingdoms. While he and Hol'anyee chose the untamed primeval crater of southern Kalimdor, his brother Livingston Marshal set off for the jungles of Stranglethorn Vale. Before parting ways, Williden scoffed at Livingston's plans, declaring he would never find anything of worth in Stranglethorn. Williden remains entirely convinced that Un'Goro's crystal deposits and ancient mysteries hold the true fortune.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Williden Marshal?",a="Williden Marshal is a human explorer and the commander of Marshal's Expedition. He led a team of researchers and adventurers into Un'Goro Crater to study its strange crystals and flora, seeking knowledge and profit.",al={"who is williden marshal","williden marshal lore","who leads marshal's refuge"}},{q="Why is the expedition holed up in a cave?",a="The expedition originally established multiple research bases down in the lowlands of Un'Goro. However, the crater's colossal predators—especially the devilsaurs and gorillas—overran the sites, forcing the survivors to flee to the northern rock ledges of Marshal's Refuge.",al={"why is the refuge in a cave","what happened to the expedition camps","why did marshal retreat"}},{q="What is Williden asking adventurers to do?",a="Williden asks capable explorers to brave the dangerous crater basin to recover supplies from their ruined camps, including abandoned food stores, delicate research equipment, and his lost expedition journal.",al={"williden quests","expedition salvation","what does williden want"}},{q="What brought Williden to Un'Goro Crater in the first place?",a="He came in search of the crater's unique resources: rare flora, mysterious colored power crystals, ancient geological secrets, and the significant financial profits that scientific discoveries would yield back home.",al={"why come to ungoro","williden marshal motivation","what is marshal researching"}},{q="Does Williden have any family?",a="Yes. He is the brother of Livingston Marshal, an explorer who ventured south into the jungles of Stranglethorn Vale, and is related to Hol'anyee. Williden famously mocked Livingston, believing Stranglethorn was worthless compared to Un'Goro.",al={"williden brother","livingston marshal","marshal family"}},{q="Is Williden Marshal aligned with the Alliance or Horde?",a="Though human, Williden runs a neutral scientific expedition out of Marshal's Refuge. He willingly accepts assistance from both Alliance and Horde adventurers willing to recover his supplies and clear threats from the crater.",al={"is williden alliance","can horde talk to williden","marshal refuge faction"}}},ang={["race:Human"]="Williden represents the far-reaching curiosity and mercantile ambition of humanity, having journeyed all the way from the Eastern Kingdoms to the untamed depths of southern Kalimdor.",["faction:Alliance"]="Though operating neutrally out of necessity in the wild crater, Williden and his core team share strong cultural and trade ties to the Alliance heartlands.",["profession:Herbalism"]="Williden's expedition was drawn to Un'Goro in large part due to the crater's unique, prehistoric vegetation that grows nowhere else on Azeroth."},kw={"devilsaurs","livingston marshal","marshals expedition","marshals refuge","power crystals","spark nilminer","ungoro crater","williden marshal"},rel={"subzone:marshal-s-refuge","zone:ungoro","zone:stranglethorn","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:alliance"},src={"Williden Marshal"}}
E["subzone:fire-plume-ridge"] = {t="subzone",n="Fire Plume Ridge",z="ungoro",s="Fire Plume Ridge is the active volcano rising directly from the center of Un'Goro Crater. Its searing slopes and subterranean magma channels fuel the crater's geysers and steam pools while playing host to fierce fire elementals.",h="Fire Plume Ridge is the active volcano rising directly from the center of Un'Goro Crater.",sec={{t="The Hearth of the Crater",b="Towering over the primeval basin of Un'Goro, Fire Plume Ridge stands in sharp contrast to the surrounding lush jungle. Lava steadily cascades down its scorched rock faces, carving a landscape of ash and basalt. Subterranean magma arteries spiderweb outward beneath the soil from the ridge, fueling the bubbling geysers and hot springs scattered across the basin. The oppressive heat here is legendary—far exceeding ordinary volcanic temperatures according to goblin measuring devices—making it perilous for ill-prepared explorers to wander without ample water and shade.",sp=0},{t="A Den of Elementals",b="The volcano is an elemental furnace teeming with living flame. Living flares and roving fire elementals patrol the glowing flows, drawn to the concentration of pure subterranean heat. Deep within a cavern near the volcanic summit resides Blazerunner, the undisputed master among Un'Goro's elemental denizens. Venturing high up the ridge means navigating both lethal heat and volatile elemental spirits that aggressively defend their fiery domain.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the volcano in the middle of Un'Goro Crater?",a="It is Fire Plume Ridge, an active volcano right in the center of Un'Goro Crater. Its molten channels feed the heat that warms the surrounding jungle and steam springs.",al={"ungoro volcano name","volcano in center of ungoro","fire plume ridge location"}},{q="Who rules the elementals at Fire Plume Ridge?",a="The peak cavern is inhabited by Blazerunner, the most powerful fire elemental in Un'Goro Crater.",al={"boss of fire plume ridge","blazerunner location","fire elemental boss ungoro"}},{q="Why is there an explorer stranded inside the ridge?",a="A goblin-allied adventurer named Ringo ventured onto the volcano to explore, but succumbed to severe heat exhaustion inside one of the southern caves, unable to escape without assistance.",al={"who is stranded in fire plume ridge","ringo ungoro","lost guy in volcano"}},{q="How does the volcano affect the rest of Un'Goro?",a="Shallow veins of magma run out from beneath Fire Plume Ridge beneath the entire crater floor, warming the earth and creating the numerous geysers, thermal vents, and steam pools found throughout the basin.",al={"why is ungoro so hot","crater geothermal activity","shallow magma veins ungoro"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="The spirits of fire burn furiously across the ridge, offering a vivid glimpse into the restless elemental powers churning beneath Kalimdor's crust.",["profession:Mining"]="The crags and heat-hardened slopes of the ridge are rich with exposed minerals, notably veins of dense Thorium formed by volcanic pressure."},kw={"blazerunner","elementals","fire plume ridge","lava","ringo","ungoro","volcano"},rel={"zone:ungoro","npc:ringo"},src={"Fire Plume Ridge"}}
E["subzone:fungal-rock"] = {t="subzone",n="Fungal Rock",z="ungoro",s="Fungal Rock is a damp, cavernous hollow carved into the northeastern cliff walls of Un'Goro Crater. Dominated by aggressive primates and thick growths of Ghost Mushrooms, it is one of the crater's most dangerous ape dens.",h="Fungal Rock is a damp, cavernous hollow carved into the northeastern cliff walls of Un'Goro Crater.",sec={{t="The Ape Den",b="Tucked behind a small waterfall and pool along Un'Goro Crater's northeastern edge, Fungal Rock serves as the primary den for the region's massive gorillas. Inside the damp, subterranean corridors, towering Un'Goro Stompers and Thunderers patrol among clusters of rare Ghost Mushrooms. The deepest recesses house territorial behemoths, including the mighty silverback U'cha and the elusive albino gorilla Uhk'loc. Beyond its primal inhabitants, curious travelers may stumble upon artificial oddities near the cave mouth, such as A-Me 01, a damaged mechanical ape abandoned by gnome researchers.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Fungal Rock?",a="Fungal Rock is a large cave system located in the northeastern wall of Un'Goro Crater. It is known for its damp environment, plentiful Ghost Mushrooms, and a dense population of hostile gorillas.",al={"where is fungal rock","what is fungal rock cave"}},{q="Who rules the apes inside Fungal Rock?",a="The cave is dominated by U'cha, a massive and powerful silverback gorilla who resides in its deepest chamber. The rare white gorilla Uhk'loc is also known to roam these caverns.",al={"who is u'cha","boss of fungal rock","fungal rock leader"}},{q="Why is there a mechanical gorilla outside the cave?",a="Near the pool outside the entrance rests A-Me 01, an engineered mechanical ape built by the gnome researcher Karna Remtravel. It broke down during field observations and awaits salvage or repair.",al={"what is a-me 01","robot gorilla ungoro","ame 01"}},{q="What valuable resources grow in Fungal Rock?",a="The cavern's damp, shaded interior provides the ideal environment for Ghost Mushrooms, making it one of the few places in southern Kalimdor where herbalists can harvest this sought-after fungus.",al={"ghost mushrooms ungoro","herbs in fungal rock"}}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="Fungal Rock is one of the premier gathering spots in Un'Goro Crater for Ghost Mushrooms, though harvesters must contend with packs of territorial gorillas to reach them.",["race:Gnome"]="Fellow gnomes may be drawn to Fungal Rock to investigate the fate of A-Me 01, Karna Remtravel's ambitious mechanical ape prototype left near the entrance pool."},kw={"a-me 01","crater","fungal rock","ghost mushroom","gorilla","u'cha","uhk'loc","un'goro"},rel={"zone:ungoro"},src={"Fungal Rock"}}
E["subzone:golakka-hot-springs"] = {t="subzone",n="Golakka Hot Springs",z="ungoro",s="Golakka Hot Springs is a geothermal basin in western Un'Goro Crater, nestled just north of Terror Run. Its bubbling pools and erupting geysers are fueled by the intense volcanic activity of nearby Fire Plume Ridge. The mineral-rich waters attract eccentric researchers, alchemists in search of exotic reagents, and wandering water elementals known as Steaming Furies.",h="Golakka Hot Springs is a geothermal basin in western Un'Goro Crater, nestled just north of Terror Run.",sec={{t="Boiling Waters and Volcanic Steam",b="Situated in the western reaches of Un'Goro Crater, the Golakka Hot Springs are a direct product of the subterranean heat radiating from Fire Plume Ridge. Scalding water bubbles continuously to the surface, shaping tiered mineral terraces and violently erupting geysers. The environment is heavily prowled by Steaming Furies, elemental manifestations born from the convergence of subterranean groundwater and volcanic heat. Despite the danger, the springs frequently draw explorers, herbalists, and researchers fascinated by the crater's unique geology.",sp=0},{t="Curious Inhabitants and Strange Chemistry",b="The unique properties of Golakka's waters have drawn interest beyond simple sightseeing. Alchemists value the geothermally enriched spring water as a potent catalytic reagent, even utilizing it in delicate concotions such as love potions. The geothermal vent also hosts quirky visitors, such as the gnome Spark Nilminer perched atop the central geyser vent, and draws the researcher Krakle, who seeks to decipher how the hot springs directly tap into the volcanic heart of the crater.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are the springs so hot?",a="The hot springs are heated by the intense volcanic system beneath Un'Goro Crater, tied directly to Fire Plume Ridge. Magma beneath the crater floor superheats subterranean water reserves, forcing boiling, mineral-rich water and steam up through geysers and terraced pools.",al={"why is water boiling","geothermal heat un'goro","fire plume connection"}},{q="What creatures live in Golakka Hot Springs?",a="The most prominent creatures patrolling the shores and pools are Steaming Furies. These are elemental spirits of living water transformed by the searing heat of the volcanic vents into roiling, volatile steam.",al={"hot springs elementals","what lives in golakka","steaming fury"}},{q="What is the water from the hot springs used for?",a="The mineral-infused water is prized by alchemists and eccentric brewers for its unique chemical properties. Notably, pristine samples taken from the springs are sought after as a vital reagent in brewing specialized concotions, including potent love potions.",al={"golakka water use","hot springs love potion","hot springs reagents"}},{q="Who is Krakle and what was he doing here?",a="Krakle is a researcher studying the geothermal relationship between Golakka Hot Springs and Fire Plume Ridge, gathering observations and temperature readings around the springs.",al={"krakle un'goro","krakle hot springs","researcher at the hot springs"}}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="The extreme geological activity provides endless fascination for gnomes like Spark Nilminer, who braves the scalding pressure vents to observe geothermal mechanics up close.",["class:Shaman"]="The hot springs showcase an intense interplay between fire and water, where the elemental clash gives rise to boiling Steaming Furies along the mineral banks."},kw={"fire plume ridge","geyser","golakka","hot springs","krakle","spark nilminer","steaming fury","terror run","un'goro"},rel={"zone:ungoro","subzone:fire-plume-ridge","subzone:terror-run"},src={"Golakka Hot Springs"}}
E["subzone:hall-of-repose-un-goro-crater"] = {t="subzone",n="Hall of Repose (Un'Goro Crater)",z="ungoro",s="The Hall of Repose is a chamber deep within the Shaper's Terrace, an ancient Titan facility carved into the cliffs of Un'Goro Crater. Its cold stone halls and cosmic architecture stand in stark contrast to the untamed, primeval jungle outside.",h="The Hall of Repose is a chamber deep within the Shaper's Terrace, an ancient Titan facility carved into the...",sec={{t="Chamber of the Makers",b="Built into the Shaper's Terrace at the northern cliffs of Un'Goro Crater, the Hall of Repose serves as a core interior chamber of the ancient Titan complex. The crater itself is widely recognized by scholars as a vast testing ground of the Makers, and structures like this hall were raised to house cosmic machinery, observation platforms, and caretakers of Azeroth's early design. Despite thousands of years passing without obvious Titan presence, the stonework remains impeccably preserved against the humid, vine-choked jungle surrounding it.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Hall of Repose?",a="It is an interior chamber of the Shaper's Terrace complex located along the northern perimeter of Un'Goro Crater. Like the rest of the terrace, it was engineered by the Titans during the ancient shaping and ordering of Azeroth.",al={"what is hall of repose","hall of repose purpose","ungoro titan room"}},{q="Who built this chamber?",a="It was crafted by the Titans or their stone creations. The smooth, immense masonry and architectural motifs match other ancient maker facilities scattered across the world.",al={"who made hall of repose","who built shapers terrace","hall of repose creators"}},{q="Why is it called the Hall of Repose?",a="The Titans and their keepers often designated chambers according to administrative, contemplative, or dormant functions. While its exact ancient designation is lost to mortal memory, the name reflects a quiet, secluded sanctum away from the chaotic ecology of the crater.",al={"why repose","name meaning hall of repose"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves fascinated by their Titan heritage, standing within the Hall of Repose offers a direct glimpse into the seamless masonry and architectural artistry of the Makers."},kw={"hall of repose","makers","shaper's terrace","shapers","titans","un'goro crater"},rel={"subzone:shaper-s-terrace","zone:ungoro"},src={"Hall of Repose (Un'Goro Crater)"}}
E["subzone:lakkari-tar-pits"] = {t="subzone",n="Lakkari Tar Pits",z="ungoro",s="The Lakkari Tar Pits are a series of foul-smelling, bubbling pools of thick black sludge in northern Un'Goro Crater. Situated just below the cliffs of Marshal's Refuge, they act as a natural death trap for unwary beasts and an incubator for hostile tar elementals.",h="The Lakkari Tar Pits are a series of foul-smelling, bubbling pools of thick black sludge in northern Un'Goro...",sec={{t="A Grasping Trap",b="The Lakkari Tar Pits dominate the low ground of northern Un'Goro Crater, directly south of Marshal's Refuge. Thick, reeking pools of pitch entrap anything careless enough to step into them, quickly bogging down beasts and adventurers alike. The protruding bones of hundreds of prehistoric creatures break the black surface, bearing witness to generations of animals sucked into the mire. Opportunistic scavengers circle the margins waiting for trapped prey to exhaust itself, while living tar beasts, lurkers, and creepers rise directly from the muck to batter interlopers.",sp=0},{t="Hidden Botanicals",b="Despite the choking conditions, the pits nurture unique life. Rare flora known as tarblossoms root deep at the bottom of the tar lakes. These flowers are prized among botanists and herbalists for their astonishing durability and vibrant appearance, though recovering them requires braving the suffocating sludge and fending off the predatory tar lords that rule the bubbling morass.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What happens if you step into the tar?",a="The pitch is extraordinarily thick and clinging. Wading into the tar immediately reduces movement speed to a crawl, making it agonizingly difficult to evade the aggressive tar elementals that patrol the surface.",al={"tar pits effect","tar slow","stepping in tar"}},{q="What creatures live in the Lakkari Tar Pits?",a="The pits are inhabited by sentient ooze and elemental life forms known as tar beasts, tar creepers, tar lurkers, and tar lords. The rare behemoth Gormashh also stalks the sludge, accompanied by local scavengers that circle the pools looking for stuck prey.",al={"tar beasts","tar pit monsters","tar creepers"}},{q="What are tarblossoms?",a="Tarblossoms are hardy, beautiful flowers that manage to grow submerged along the beds of the tar pits. Because the viscous pitch preserves and shields them, they are durable and sought after by naturalists, though exceptionally hazardous to harvest.",al={"tar blossom","tar flowers","un'goro tar flower"}},{q="Where are the Lakkari Tar Pits located?",a="They are located in northern Un'Goro Crater, sitting directly in the basin beneath the cliffside outpost of Marshal's Refuge.",al={"tar pits location","where is lakkari","how to find tar pits"}}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="The pits are infamous for the rare tarblossom, an elusive flower that thrives deep under the suffocating pitch.",["class:Hunter"]="Keep pets on firm ground near Lakkari; any creature caught in the thick sludge becomes an immobilized target for predatory tar lurkers."},kw={"creeper","gormashh","lakkari","marshal's refuge","tar beast","tar pits","tarblossom","un'goro"},rel={"zone:ungoro","subzone:marshal-s-refuge"},src={"Lakkari Tar Pits"}}
E["subzone:marshal-s-refuge"] = {t="subzone",n="Marshal's Refuge",z="ungoro",s="Marshal's Refuge is a precarious, neutral haven tucked into the northern cliffs of Un'Goro Crater. Established by Williden Marshal and his expedition party, it serves as an emergency redoubt after the basin's primeval beasts routed their lower camps.",h="Marshal's Refuge is a precarious, neutral haven tucked into the northern cliffs of Un'Goro Crater.",sec={{t="A Precarious Perch",b="When Williden and Hol'anyee Marshal led their expedition into Un'Goro Crater, they drastically underestimated the ferocity of its prehistoric denizens. After their initial base camps were repeatedly overrun by rampaging beasts, the battered survivors scrambled up into the cavernous northern cliffside to escape slaughter. Re-established as Marshal's Refuge, the camp clings high above the jungle floor, offering the only stable resting ground, basic supplies, and flight masters for weary explorers in the northern crater.",sp=0},{t="A Crossroads of Curiosity",b="Because Un'Goro Crater contains ancient biological wonders and mysterious crystal formations, Marshal's Refuge attracts a motley band of researchers, fortune seekers, and eccentric wanderers. Both Alliance and Horde naturalists, including tauren emissaries and gnomish tinkers, share the crowded ledge alongside the surviving Marshal crew. From here, scouts strike out toward volcanic summits like Fire Plume Ridge or bubbling landmarks like the Golakka Hot Springs, hoping to catalog the primordial wilderness before it consumes them.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why was Marshal's Refuge built so high up the cliff?",a="The Marshal expedition originally established camps lower in the basin, but Un'Goro's ferocious dinosaurs and aggressive creatures constantly trampled and overran them. The survivors retreated up the northern rock wall to gain a defensible vantage point safely out of reach of the larger beasts.",al={"why is it in a cave","marshals refuge location","why cliffside camp"}},{q="Is Marshal's Refuge friendly to both Horde and Alliance?",a="Yes. It operates as a neutral outpost. The primeval perils of Un'Goro Crater make faction rivalries an unaffordable luxury, so members of both factions mingle here peacefully to resupply and trade research.",al={"is marshals refuge neutral","can horde go here","can alliance go here"}},{q="Who leads the encampment?",a="The outpost is led by Williden Marshal and Hol'anyee Marshal, the figures who organized the ill-fated Marshal Expeditions into the crater.",al={"who is in charge","who runs marshals refuge","camp leader"}},{q="What services are available at the Refuge?",a="The refuge provides essential survival necessities in the remote basin, including flight masters for both factions, basic trade merchants, repair services, and a gathering spot for researchers offering bounties and investigations across the crater.",al={"flight path","repairs","vendors"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="Perched safely above the caldera floor, the Refuge offers hunters a vantage point to study Un'Goro's rarest and deadliest beasts before descending into the tracking grounds.",["race:Gnome"]="Gnome scholars and field-engineers find the Refuge an ideal outpost for testing apparatuses on the crater's bizarre power crystals and volatile geysers."},kw={"cave","expedition","hol'anyee","marshal's refuge","un'goro crater","williden marshal"},rel={"zone:ungoro","subzone:fire-plume-ridge","subzone:golakka-hot-springs","topic:gnome","topic:tauren","topic:dwarf"},src={"Marshal's Refuge"}}
E["subzone:marshlands"] = {t="subzone",n="Marshlands",z="ungoro",s="The Marshlands is a sprawling, sodden marsh occupying the southeastern reach of Un'Goro Crater. Sitting directly at the base of the winding ramp down from Tanaris, it is often the first wilderness newcomers witness upon entering the primeval basin.",h="The Marshlands is a sprawling, sodden marsh occupying the southeastern reach of Un'Goro Crater.",sec={{t="Gateway to the Crater",b="Descending the steep trail from the arid expanse of Tanaris brings travelers directly into the humid mire of the Marshlands. Navigating anywhere else along the sheer crater rim invites a lethal fall, making this treacherous swath of wetlands the primary threshold into Un'Goro. Dense canopies, standing water, and mud conceal abundant packs of fierce raptors, including venomous varieties that stalk the reeds. Amid the damp clearings, explorers can find Blue Power Crystals scattered across the earth, unique to this quarter of the crater.",sp=0},{t="Encampments in the Bog",b="Despite the constant danger of predators, several solitary wilderness experts maintain outposts across the marsh. Perched upon a prominent earthen mound, the tauren Torwa Pathfinder and his companion Garl Stormclaw keep watch over the primeval fauna after navigating the basin by canoe. Across the wetlands, the troll Mor'vek studies and trains native ravasaurs, while toward the northern fringes, the night elf Ithis Moonwarden monitors the aggressive sprouting of young bloodpetal plants.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is the Marshlands usually the first area people see in Un'Goro?",a="The sheer cliffs surrounding Un'Goro Crater make entering from any point other than the southeastern pass in Tanaris almost certainly fatal. The ramp leads straight down into the Marshlands, forcing all terrestrial travelers through its sodden reaches.",al={"how to enter ungoro","entering ungoro crater","marshlands entrance"}},{q="What creatures are most common here?",a="The marsh is notorious for dense populations of raptors. These include both standard hunting raptors and deadly, venomous species capable of overwhelming unwary explorers in the thick brush.",al={"marshlands beasts","marshlands raptors","what lives here"}},{q="What unique resources are found in the Marshlands?",a="The Marshlands is the only place in Un'Goro Crater where Blue Power Crystals naturally form. These glowing mineral shards are prized by researchers studying the mysterious crystalline pylons scattered throughout the basin.",al={"blue power crystals","marshlands crystals","blue crystals ungoro"}},{q="Who is Torwa Pathfinder?",a="Torwa Pathfinder is an experienced tauren hunter stationed on a high mound within the Marshlands alongside Garl Stormclaw. He observes the crater's ecology and guides capable adventurers against Un'Goro's most ferocious beasts.",al={"torwa","torwa pathfinder camp"}},{q="Can the ravasaurs here be tamed or trained?",a="Yes. Mor'vek, a troll living in the Marshlands, specializes in handling and raising native ravasaurs, offering insight into their aggressive nature and instincts.",al={"ravasaur trainer","morvek","train ravasaur"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="The Marshlands provides an immediate testing ground for wilderness survival, populated by swift raptors, venomous predators, and rare beasts guided by seasoned trackers like Torwa Pathfinder.",["profession:Herbalism"]="The northern edges of the marsh are choked with aggressive bloodpetal saplings and damp foliage, making it a prime site for observing hostile, mobile plant life."},kw={"blue power crystals","marshlands","mor'vek","raptors","ravasaur","tanaris","torwa pathfinder","un'goro"},rel={"zone:ungoro","zone:tanaris","npc:torwa-pathfinder"},src={"Marshlands"}}
E["subzone:roiling-gardens"] = {t="subzone",n="Roiling Gardens",z="ungoro",s="The Roiling Gardens is an overgrown, restless stretch of Un'Goro Crater lying just north of the Marshlands. Dominated by aggressive Bloodpetals and bizarre sporous blooms, the area is teetering on ecological collapse while hiding the remnants of an abandoned expedition camp.",h="The Roiling Gardens is an overgrown, restless stretch of Un'Goro Crater lying just north of the Marshlands.",sec={{t="A Garden Out of Control",b="Situated directly north of the central Marshlands, the Roiling Gardens earned its name from the sheer, unsettling vitality of its vegetation. The local trees are smothered under a choking blanket of aggressive vines and strange flowers, while massive, sporous blossoms erupt across the soil. Worst of all are the predatory Bloodpetal plants, whose surging population threatens to completely consume the local ecosystem. The rapid, unchecked growth here has deeply upset the natural balance of Un'Goro, turning a vibrant habitat into a hostile thicket.",sp=0},{t="Forgotten Expeditions and Strange Minerals",b="Before establishing Marshal's Refuge in the safety of northern caverns, Williden Marshal's expedition attempted to camp in these very gardens. The increasingly violent plant life and dangerous environment forced a frantic retreat, so sudden that crates of supplies were left scattered among the roots. Aside from its aggressive flora and abandoned gear, the Roiling Gardens is uniquely known as the primary gathering ground for Green Power Crystals, enigmatic minerals scattered across the dirt that hum with primal Titan energies.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What makes the Roiling Gardens dangerous?",a="The area is infested with hostile, carnivorous Bloodpetal plants that have aggressively multiplied. Giant sporous blossoms and choking vines have rapidly overwhelmed the native flora, making navigation perilous for anyone walking off the beaten track.",al={"why is roiling gardens dangerous","roiling gardens threats"}},{q="Why is there an abandoned camp here?",a="The camp belonged to Williden Marshal and his expedition before they relocated north to Marshal's Refuge. The escalating danger from the ravenous plants and wildlife forced them to abandon the site in a hurry, leaving supplies such as crates of foodstuffs behind.",al={"abandoned camp roiling gardens","foodstuffs crate","marshal camp"}},{q="What kind of crystals are found in the Roiling Gardens?",a="The Roiling Gardens is the sole region in Un'Goro Crater where Green Power Crystals can be found lying on the ground. These crystals are sought after by researchers studying the ancient pylons scattered throughout the crater.",al={"green crystals ungoro","roiling gardens crystals"}},{q="Where are the Roiling Gardens located?",a="The gardens lie in the central portion of Un'Goro Crater, directly north of the Marshlands and south of the northern bluffs leading toward Marshal's Refuge.",al={"roiling gardens location","where is roiling gardens"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="The wild, predatory overgrowth of the Bloodpetals in the Roiling Gardens serves as an urgent reminder of what happens when natural balance is corrupted or pushed beyond its limits.",["profession:Herbalism"]="The rich, moist soil and bizarre runaway plant growth make the Roiling Gardens a dense, albeit dangerous, landscape for gathering rare flora."},kw={"bloodpetals","crate of foodstuffs","green power crystals","marshal's refuge","marshlands","roiling gardens","un'goro"},rel={"zone:ungoro","subzone:marshlands","subzone:marshal-s-refuge"},src={"Roiling Gardens"}}
E["subzone:screaming-reaches"] = {t="subzone",n="Screaming Reaches",z="ungoro",s="The Screaming Reaches is a rugged territory along the northwestern rim of Un'Goro Crater, famous for the deafening shrieks of the pterrordax that wheel overhead. Beyond its nesting winged reptiles, the area holds the only known deposits of Yellow Power Crystals in the crater and houses the winding ramp leading into the desolate wastes of Silithus.",h="The Screaming Reaches is a rugged territory along the northwestern rim of Un'Goro Crater, famous for the...",sec={{t="The Roost of the Pterrordax",b="Stretching west from the Mossy Pile toward the crater's northwestern cliffs, the Screaming Reaches earned its moniker from the endless cries of the predatory pterrordax nesting across the rocky ledges. Travelers venturing beneath the canopy must watch both the dense undergrowth and the open sky, as these winged terrors swoop down upon anything entering their hunting grounds. The slopes also sparkle with vibrant, hum-charged Yellow Power Crystals, making the dangerous cliffs a frequent destination for naturalists and crystal hunters studying the strange energies coursing through Un'Goro.",sp=0},{t="Passage to Silithus",b="Tucked away in the far northwestern corner of the Reaches lies an incline cutting up through the caldera wall. Mirroring the southern descent from Tanaris, this stone pathway forms the sole natural exit connecting Un'Goro Crater directly to the arid barrens of Silithus. While the crater floor bursts with primeval life, the top of this steep slope opens into harsh desert winds and swirling dust, marking the border between two vastly different Kalimdor wildernesses.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is this area called the Screaming Reaches?",a="The region is named after the constant, piercing screeches of the pterrordax that nest along the northwestern cliffs. Their shrill calls echo continuously across the rock faces and forest canopy.",al={"screaming reaches name meaning","why called screaming reaches","why screaming"}},{q="Where does the mountain ramp in the northwest lead?",a="The winding stone ramp in the far northwestern edge of the Screaming Reaches leads up out of Un'Goro Crater and straight into the windblown desert of Silithus.",al={"screaming reaches ramp","path in northwest ungoro","exit to silithus"}},{q="What kind of power crystals grow here?",a="The Screaming Reaches is the exclusive source of Yellow Power Crystals in Un'Goro Crater. These glowing crystal formations can be gathered off the ground and used in conjunction with the crater's mysterious pylon devices.",al={"yellow crystals ungoro","screaming reaches crystals","where to find yellow power crystal"}},{q="What threats should travelers expect here?",a="The area is heavily populated by territorial pterrordax circling above and nesting on the ground. Visitors must keep an eye on the skies to avoid being ambushed by diving reptiles while traversing the uneven terrain.",al={"screaming reaches mobs","what monsters live here","screaming reaches dangers"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="The high vantage points and abundant pterrordax make the Reaches a prime study ground for beast-trackers looking to understand the habits of primeval aerial predators."},kw={"mossy pile","pterrordax","screaming reaches","silithus ramp","ungoro","yellow power crystal"},rel={"zone:ungoro","zone:silithus"},src={"Screaming Reaches"}}
E["subzone:shaper-s-terrace"] = {t="subzone",n="Shaper's Terrace",z="ungoro",s="Perched high on the northern bluffs above Marshal's Refuge, the Shaper's Terrace is a mysterious overlook marked by ancient titan architecture. It is named in honor of Khaz'goroth the Shaper and bears quiet witness to the primordial experiments that shaped Un'Goro Crater.",h="Perched high on the northern bluffs above Marshal's Refuge, the Shaper's Terrace is a mysterious overlook...",sec={{t="A Legacy of the Titans",b="Overlooking the lush, prehistoric basin of Un'Goro Crater, the Shaper's Terrace holds monumental stone edifices left behind by the titans. Believed to be dedicated to Khaz'goroth the Shaper, this high plateau stands as a testament to the celestial architects who cultivated the crater as a living laboratory for early life on Azeroth. From these elevated stones, ancient entities once observed and directed the flora and fauna below. While largely inaccessible from the crater floor, its cold stone arches and massive metallic plinths stand in stark, enigmatic contrast to the untamed wilderness thriving directly beneath them.",sp=0},{t="The Dormant Waygate",b="Dominating the terrace is an inert Waygate, constructed of intricate titan craftsmanship. Similar in make to titanic mechanisms scattered across ancient lands, this archway hints at cosmic pathways spanning across worlds or continents, though its mechanisms remain dormant to ordinary travelers in the crater. Its presence above Marshal's Refuge continues to fuel the curiosity of scholars, explorers, and dwarves seeking to piece together how the titans connected their grand design across Azeroth.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Shaper's Terrace?",a="The Shaper's Terrace is an elevated titan site located along the northern bluffs of Un'Goro Crater, directly above Marshal's Refuge. It features stone edifices and an inert gateway tied to the titans who once shaped the land.",al={"shapers terrace","what is this terrace","ungoro terrace"}},{q="Who was the 'Shaper'?",a="The terrace refers to Khaz'goroth the Shaper, one of the titanic creators who helped craft and cultivate the world of Azeroth in the deep past.",al={"who is the shaper","khazgoroth","who made shapers terrace"}},{q="Can you reach the terrace from Un'Goro Crater?",a="The northern terrace sits high on the cliffs and cannot be reached by normal climbing paths from the basin floor. Those who find themselves upon its heights can descend toward Marshal's Refuge, but scaling the cliffs up is virtually impossible on foot.",al={"how to get to shapers terrace","how do i reach shapers terrace"}},{q="What is the large stone arch located here?",a="It is a titan Waygate, an ancient teleportation conduit designed by the makers to link their testing facilities across vast distances, though it currently sits quiet.",al={"arch on shapers terrace","portal in shapers terrace","what is the gateway"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves pursuing their titan ancestry, the Shaper's Terrace provides another tantalizing glimpse of Khaz'goroth's architecture and the grand works of the creators.",["class:Mage"]="The dormant Waygate on the terrace showcases portal magic and spatial anchoring on a monumental, divine scale far beyond mortal conjuration."},kw={"crater","khaz'goroth","marshal's refuge","shaper","shaper's terrace","titan","un'goro","waygate"},rel={"zone:ungoro","subzone:marshal-s-refuge","topic:titan"},src={"Shaper's Terrace"}}
E["subzone:slithering-scar"] = {t="subzone",n="Slithering Scar",z="ungoro",s="The Slithering Scar is a sprawling silithid hive dominating the southern cliffs of Un'Goro Crater. Home to the aggressive Gorishi swarm, its excavated tunnels and organic spires represent a dangerous insectoid encroachment into the primeval basin.",h="The Slithering Scar is a sprawling silithid hive dominating the southern cliffs of Un'Goro Crater.",sec={{t="The Gorishi Hive",b="Gouged into the red earth and rock of southern Un'Goro, the Slithering Scar stands as an alien intrusion against the lush prehistoric landscape. The hive is controlled by the Gorishi silithid, an organized strain of insectoids that have honeycombed the cliffs with damp burrows and egg chambers. Within these subterranean warrens, workers and tunnelers nurture vast clutches of eggs and grubs alongside towering wasp broods. More alarmingly, the colony cultivates fledgling silithid colossi, monstrous behemoths intended to carve an uncontested path through the crater's ecology. Strange crystalline formations nestled within the hive pulse with unnatural resonance, acting as focal points for the colony's dark, coordinated will.",sp=0},{t="A Missing Ward",b="Scholars and explorers who traverse the perimeter of Un'Goro often notice a disturbing anomaly regarding the hive's location. While ancient crystalline pylons stand sentinel across the northern, eastern, and western boundaries of the basin, the southern reaches possess no such pillar. It is precisely in this unprotected gap that the Gorishi have burrowed inward from the neighboring deserts. Whether the silithid purposefully undermined a forgotten southern ward or simply invaded where the crater's primordial wards were weakest remains an unsettling mystery to those watching their rapid expansion.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Slithering Scar?",a="It is a silithid hive complex carved into the southern cliff walls of Un'Goro Crater, inhabited by the Gorishi swarm.",al={"what is this place","slithering scar overview","ungoro bug hive"}},{q="What are the silithid doing here?",a="The Gorishi swarm is digging vast subterranean tunnels, tending nursery chambers full of grubs and eggs, and raising massive silithid colossi to establish dominance over the crater.",al={"why are bugs here","silithid purpose ungoro","gorishi goal"}},{q="Why is there no pylon in the south like the other regions?",a="While the northern, eastern, and western edges of Un'Goro are marked by ancient crystal pylons, the southern cliff has none. The Slithering Scar emerged precisely where this protective boundary is missing.",al={"missing southern pylon","why no south pylon","where is the south pylon"}},{q="What dangerous creatures inhabit the hive?",a="Aside from legions of workers, reavers, and stingers, the Scar is stalked by developing colossi and notoriously ferocious broodmothers like Clutchmother Zavas.",al={"hive bosses","notable bugs","clutchmother zavas"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="The aggressive spread of the Gorishi hive threatens the delicate, untamed vitality of the crater, demanding vigilance against unnatural infestation."},kw={"clutchmother zavas","colossus","gorishi","hive","silithid","slithering scar","ungoro"},rel={"zone:ungoro","npc:grub"},src={"Slithering Scar"}}
E["subzone:terror-run"] = {t="subzone",n="Terror Run",z="ungoro",s="Terror Run is a perilous swath of land situated in the southwestern reaches of Un'Goro Crater, directly west of the insectoid hives of the Slithering Scar. True to its fearsome name, the territory is stalked by predatory beasts, ranging from massive devilsaurs to ravenous diemetradons and swooping pterrordax.",h="Terror Run is a perilous swath of land situated in the southwestern reaches of Un'Goro Crater, directly west...",sec={{t="A Hunt in the Open",b="Stretching across the southwestern shelf of Un'Goro Crater, Terror Run lives up to its ominous reputation. Fierce pterrordax wheel through the humid air above while massive diemetradons, stegodons, and apex devilsaurs roam the low brush below. The territory sits directly in the shadow of the mountainous rim, wedged uncomfortably close to the chittering alien mounds of the Slithering Scar. Along the eastern edge of the flats lie the ruined remnants of a camp left behind by Williden Marshal's expedition, a sobering reminder of researchers who were caught unprepared when the crater's primeval predators closed in.",sp=0},{t="Red Crystals and Ancient Predators",b="Beyond the sheer concentration of hungry fauna, Terror Run draws naturalists and adventurers alike for a geological rarity: it is the primary ground in the crater where curious Red Power Crystals emerge from the fertile soil. The crimson formations hum with primeval energy akin to the blue, green, and yellow crystals found elsewhere in the basin. Surviving long enough to gather them, however, means contending with the sovereign hunters of the plains—including nesting apex devilsaurs that brook no trespassers in the deep south.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is this area called Terror Run?",a="The name reflects the deadly concentration of apex predators that stalk this open corridor. Between massive devilsaurs, territorial diemetradons, and watchful pterrordax soaring overhead, anyone crossing the flats on foot is liable to find themselves sprinting for their life.",al={"terror run name meaning","why terror run","who named terror run"}},{q="What can be found here besides dangerous beasts?",a="Terror Run is the only region in Un'Goro Crater where Red Power Crystals can be gathered from the earth. You can also find an abandoned research camp on its eastern edge, discarded by Williden Marshal's expedition during their perilous survey of the crater.",al={"what is in terror run","terror run crystals","terror run resources"}},{q="What is the abandoned camp on the eastern edge?",a="The abandoned campsite belonged to members of Williden Marshal's expedition. The scientists and explorers were forced to abandon their research equipment and flee when the local wildlife overwhelmed their position.",al={"marshals camp terror run","abandoned research camp","lost expedition camp"}},{q="Where does Terror Run lie in relation to other landmarks?",a="It spans southwestern Un'Goro Crater, situated directly west of the silithid-infested hives known as the Slithering Scar and south of the central volcano, Fire Plume Ridge.",al={"terror run location","where is terror run"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="The vast plains of Terror Run are a lethal proving ground, boasting some of the fiercest beasts in Kalimdor—from swift raptors and savage pterrordax to towering devilsaurs."},kw={"devilsaur","diemetradon","marshal expedition","pterrordax","red power crystal","slithering scar","terror run","ungoro"},rel={"zone:ungoro","subzone:slithering-scar"},src={"Terror Run"}}
E["zone:ungoro"] = {t="zone",n="Un'Goro Crater",z="ungoro",s="Un'Goro Crater is a sunken, primordial jungle tucked between the arid wastes of Tanaris and Silithus. Dominated by roaming dinosaurs, living elementals, and a central volcano, this lush caldera is filled with ancient Titan relics and power crystals whose origins remain a profound mystery.",h="Un'Goro Crater is a sunken, primordial jungle tucked between the arid wastes of Tanaris and Silithus.",sec={{t="The God Lands",b="Sandwiched between desert expanses, Un'Goro Crater defies the geography of southern Kalimdor. Ancient night elf records detailing the War of the Shifting Sands note that the insectoid Qiraji were turned back at the crater's edges, unable to penetrate what their tongue named the 'God Lands.' Scholars theorize the caldera served as a testing ground or ancient dwelling for the Titans during the shaping of Kalimdor. Stone pylons rise along the ridges, humming with energy, while crystal formations of blue, red, green, and yellow sprout through the primeval earth.",sp=0},{t="A Savage Ecosystem",b="Un'Goro contains no cities, towns, or native humanoid societies. Instead, life thrives in an untamed, primeval state. Apex devilsaurs stalk the flats of Terror Run, predatory bloodpetals lash out in the marshlands, and oozes creep across the tar pits of Lakkari. At the heart of the crater looms Fire Plume Ridge, an active volcanic peak teeming with hostile fire elementals led by the entity Blazerunner. For explorers and skinners, the basin offers unmatched natural wealth—including the coveted hides of devilsaurs—provided one survives the food chain.",sp=0},{t="Marshal's Refuge",b="Civilized presence in the crater is limited almost entirely to Marshal's Refuge, an elevated camp tucked into the northern cliffs. Led by Williden Marshal, an expedition of scientists, naturalists, and fortune seekers attempted to catalogue the basin's treasures only to be battered by the monstrous wildlife and driven to high ground. Today, the refuge serves as an embattled staging ground for intrepid travelers studying the crater's mysterious power crystals, mapping volcanic activity, and keeping a watchful eye on encroaching silithid swarms breaching the southern ridges.",sp=0}},faq={{q="How do you get into Un'Goro Crater?",a="Travelers can enter via natural ramps leading down the crater walls: one accessible from the southwestern corner of Tanaris near Thistleshrub Valley, and another leading in from northeastern Silithus. While reckless adventurers sometimes leap down the cliffs, the fall is fatal without magical assistance. Marshal's Refuge in the north provides flight connections to Gadgetzan and Cenarion Hold.",al={"how to enter ungoro","ungoro entrance","how to reach ungoro crater"}},{q="What are the colored power crystals used for?",a="Scattered across the jungle floor are red, blue, green, and yellow Power Crystals. With guidance from the gnome researcher J.D. Collie at Marshal's Refuge, explorers can decipher instructions for using these crystals at the Northern, Eastern, and Western Pylons. Combining specific colors at the appropriate pylons harnesses latent Titan energies to fashion defensive or restorative charms.",al={"ungoro crystals","red blue green yellow crystals ungoro","power pylons"}},{q="Why is Un'Goro lush despite being surrounded by deserts?",a="Scholars believe Un'Goro's unnatural vibrancy is artificial, stemming from the Titans who shaped the world. Titanic conduits, warm volcanic geothermal activity from Fire Plume Ridge, and ancient ley energy nourish an isolated, hyper-accelerated ecosystem that resists the arid conditions of neighbouring Tanaris and Silithus.",al={"why is ungoro a jungle","ungoro desert connection","how does ungoro have plants"}},{q="Why did the Qiraji call this place the 'God Lands'?",a="According to tablets translated from the War of the Shifting Sands, the insect swarms halted their advance at the crater's threshold. Geologist Larksbane's translations reveal the Qiraji viewed the basin as the domain of the Titans—specifically referencing ancient creators like Aman'Thul—whose lingering wards prevented the Swarm from claiming the region.",al={"god lands meaning","qiraji ungoro","why couldn't silithid take ungoro"}},{q="What is Un'Goro Soil used for?",a="Piles of rich, potent dirt rest across the crater basin. When harvested, this soil can be paired with Tharlendris seeds in an Evergreen Pouch to cultivate Morrowgrain, a mystical herb intensely sought after by researchers in Thunder Bluff, Darnassus, and the Cenarion Circle.",al={"ungoro soil sample","what does ungoro soil do","morrowgrain soil"}},{q="Are there any humanoid settlements or dungeons here?",a="There are no instances, dungeons, or indigenous humanoid societies in Un'Goro Crater. The only lasting settlement is Marshal's Refuge, a small expedition outpost on the northern rim. Beyond isolated hermit hunters or lost explorers, the rest of the caldera is entirely wild.",al={"ungoro dungeons","who lives in ungoro","humanoids in ungoro"}}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="The rich moisture of the basin sustains rare flora, serving as one of the few places in Kalimdor where Blindweed, Dreamfoil, and Golden Sansam flourish together alongside Firebloom on the volcano's slopes.",["profession:Mining"]="The sheer crater walls and the crags of Fire Plume Ridge are dense with Mithril Deposits and Rich Thorium Veins, making the zone a premier destination for high-end ore.",["class:Druid"]="Cenarion Circle druids study Un'Goro's isolated ecosystem and harvest its rich soil to propagate Morrowgrain, seeking to understand the pure, untamed life force sustaining the caldera.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance naturalists rally around Williden Marshal and J.D. Collie at Marshal's Refuge, racing to decipher the Titan pylons while safeguarding Darnassus researchers gathering soil samples.",["faction:Horde"]="Horde adventurers often arrive via Tanaris to test their prowess against legendary devilsaurs and assist the herbalists of Thunder Bluff in cultivating Morrowgrain from Un'Goro's primeval dirt."},kw={"devilsaur","fire plume ridge","god lands","lakkari","marshal's refuge","power crystals","torwa pathfinder","ungoro","ungoro crater"},rel={"subzone:marshal-s-refuge","subzone:fire-plume-ridge","subzone:lakkari-tar-pits","subzone:terror-run","zone:tanaris","zone:silithus","npc:williden-marshal","topic:titan"},src={"Un'Goro Crater (Classic)","Un'Goro Crater"}}
